# Sent to buildkit when building ./Dockerfile from the project root. Keep
# this narrow: everything cargo doesn't need for `--package sunbeam-proxy`
# gets stripped so we don't ship the target/ cache or large non-Rust trees.
#
# If you add a new path-patched Rust dep in the root Cargo.toml, make sure
# the directory is NOT listed here — otherwise cargo will fail to resolve it.

# Build artifacts
target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/

# VCS / editor / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.worktrees/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
.omc/

# Docs / proofs — not needed for cargo build
*.md
**/*.md
lean4/
docs/

# Non-Rust top-level trees and files that the workspace never references.
forks/
owned-forks/
research/
engines/
infra/
k8s/
scripts/
*.zip
session_*.zip
sunbeam.yaml
cloud-init-multipass-dev.yaml
lefthook.yml

# 3p/ trees stay fully included — the root Cargo.toml `[patch.crates-io]`
# rewrites tokio, mio, and every path-patched crate to local paths in 3p/.
# Excluding any of them breaks cargo workspace resolution.
#
# apps/ and libs/ likewise stay included — the root Cargo.toml lists
# workspace members under apps/sunbeam-meet/ etc., so cargo fails to parse
# the workspace if any member directory is missing. We shed size via the
# **/node_modules/ and **/target/ globs above, which covers the JS bulk.
